ive with the bills but  when you when you combine jonathan  taylor's running ability at 235 yards  on on uh sunday against the jaguars and  that defense when it's firing on all  cylinders who knows what the colts could  do and you know it was the bills beating  the dolphins that gave the colts their  ticket to the season the colts can show  their gratitude by going to buffalo on  saturday and ending prematurely the  bills playoff party i doubt that that's  going to happen but i'll tell you what  the culture when the colts are are  hitting  as i said on all cylinders they're as  dangerous as anyone in the afc  potentially okay rookie of the week time  mds who do you have  i have jerry judy of the broncos and  i've been a little down on him this year  i felt like if you compare his  production to that of some of the  receivers drafted after him he comes up  a little short but i have to say  i was watching that game i don't think  many people were against the raiders he  had a 92 yard touchdown that was  actually the longest reception in the  nfl all season finished with 140 yards  and really showed the promise that he  has and i'm going to be interested to  see  this year in denver with john elway  stepping away  what will the new gm do how how will the  new gm build this team how how much  independence will the new gm have to go  in a different direction than john elway  all of those are interesting questions  to me but one thing i think is very  clear is they do have a good young wide  receiver in place in jerry judy  mds the colts were running all over the  jaguars and suddenly they forgot about  jonathan taylor and then they came back  to him and he showed what they had been  missing in the middle of that game it  might have been a bigger blowout than  what it turned out to be if they relied  on jonathan taylor in the middle part of  that game but he still finished with 253  yards it set a franchise record edran  james had the old record of 219 in the  year 2000 a